From 72d4cc39a4b9906fd035da898e50882fba7417fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:33:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add daily admin digest email, excluding seeded/test data
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New scheduled job (server/index.ts) sends one email a day to
theyceylonx@gmail.com (overridable via DIGEST_RECIPIENT_EMAIL) at
8:00 AM Asia/Colombo — computed directly against Sri Lanka's fixed
UTC+5:30 offset rather than a timezone database, since it has no DST.
Reports new signups, new trips (regular + Quick Trips, labeled), and
running totals, matching the brief's copy. A requireAdmin-gated
POST /api/admin/digest/send-now (adminRoutes.ts) triggers the same
path on demand for testing without waiting for the schedule.

The counts exclude seeded/test data, which needed a real mechanism —
none existed. Adds users.isTestData (shared/schema.ts), set
automatically by scripts/seed-trips.ts on its 5 seed users (with a
backfill for users it already created in an earlier run), plus a
TEST_ACCOUNT_EMAILS env var for the admin's own manual test accounts,
following the same allowlist pattern SUPERADMIN_EMAILS already uses in
server/auth/passport.ts. server/utils/testDataFilter.ts resolves both
into one excluded-user-id set; trips and quick trips need no separate
flag since every row has a required organizerId to filter on.
server/services/digestService.ts holds the stat queries,
server/auth/email.ts the send/template — same split already used for
sendWelcomeEmail and the DB layer.

Needs `npm run db:push` in Replit for the new isTestData column before
this can run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
